{"term":"madam","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:6e785c4eb63d018e65","definition":"A polite form of address for a woman or lady.","example":"Mrs Grey wondered if the outfit she was trying on made her look fat. The sales assistant just said, “It suits you, madam”.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bemadam","dear Sir or Madam","Madam and Eve","madamhood","madamish","madamji","Madam President","troll madam"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/madam#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a326c3a73c6485aac9","definition":"The mistress of a household.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["dame","woman","lady","matron","mistress"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bemadam","dear Sir or Madam","Madam and Eve","madamhood","madamish","madamji","Madam President","troll madam"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/madam#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ad0a4131b261f87a08","definition":"A conceited or quarrelsome girl.","example":"Selina kept pushing and shoving during musical chairs. The nursery school teacher said she was a bad-tempered little madam.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"colloquial","register":"colloquial","wordFamily":["bemadam","dear Sir or Madam","Madam and Eve","madamhood","madamish","madamji","Madam President","troll madam"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/madam#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b3ceef37e630a8d66b","definition":"A woman who runs a brothel, particularly one that specializes in finding prostitutes for rich and important clients.","example":"After she grew too old to work as a prostitute, she became a madam.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["abbess","bawd","lady abbess","nookie-bookie","whoremistress","brothelkeeper"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"slang","register":"slang","wordFamily":["bemadam","dear Sir or Madam","Madam and Eve","madamhood","madamish","madamji","Madam President","troll madam"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/madam#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f5471f135135d69418","definition":"A hated or contemptuous woman; used as a general term of abuse","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"India, derogatory, slang","register":"India, derogatory, slang","wordFamily":["bemadam","dear Sir or Madam","Madam and Eve","madamhood","madamish","madamji","Madam President","troll madam"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/madam#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ea2be0a02280bfdc10","definition":"To address as \"madam\".","example":"Madam me no Madam, but learn to retrench your vvords; and ſay Mam; as yes Mam, and no Mam, as other Ladies VVomen do. Madam! 'tis a year in pronouncing.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["bemadam","dear Sir or Madam","Madam and Eve","madamhood","madamish","madamji","Madam President","troll madam","pimp","pimping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/madam#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bb9183fc9487e7b61d","definition":"To be a madam; to run (a brothel).","example":"The writer has never accepted the criterion “will it make money?” He has known that the application of such an irrelevancy to any of the arts and sciences resulted in sterility, error and waste. But what is more important, the writer will not pretend that this is not so. He will not pretend that the money criterion is a valid point of reference. The result has been that the writer has been kicked around from furnished room to the luxurious offices of advertising agencies and those palaces of prostitution which are madamed by public relations counsellors.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive, rare","register":"ambitransitive, rare","wordFamily":["bemadam","dear Sir or Madam","Madam and Eve","madamhood","madamish","madamji","Madam President","troll madam","pimp","pimping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/madam#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9692e1075a263d4db1","definition":"Alternative letter-case form of madam.","example":"The conſtant queſtion, upon her offering to ſtir abroad, was, where are you going Madam? To ſee the King my papa, replied the Princeſs. That cannot be Madam. No? why ſo? It is not the Etiquette. — And thus, if ſhe had a mind to viſit any of the Mesdames, the king’s ſiſters or aunts, ſhe was always told, it was not the Etiquette.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"alt-of","register":"alt-of","wordFamily":["bemadam","dear Sir or Madam","Madam and Eve","madamhood","madamish","madamji","Madam President","troll madam","pimp","pimping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Madam#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b568ae9f85f84aca48","definition":"A polite form of address and title, abbreviated Mdm, used before a (usually middle-aged) adult or elderly woman's surname, full name or given name if she does not have a family name.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Singapore","register":"Singapore","wordFamily":["bemadam","dear Sir or Madam","Madam and Eve","madamhood","madamish","madamji","Madam President","troll madam","pimp","pimping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Madam#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈmædəm/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a1/En-au-madam.ogg/En-au-madam.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["bemadam","dear Sir or Madam","Madam and Eve","madamhood","madamish","madamji","Madam President","troll madam","pimp","pimping"]}